{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1456070-celerity-4-5-and-defence-in-ranged-combats","id":1456070,"title":"Celerity 4, 5 and defence in ranged combats.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-08-03T07:05:18-07:00","id":1456070,"title":"<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/icons/icon5.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" /> Celerity 4, 5 and defence in ranged combats.","content":"<span style=\"color:#050505\"><span style=\"font-family:system-ui\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\"> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\">Hello.<br /> I have a question on the manual (V5).<br /> <br /> Basically, Celerity 4 (and 5) has powers that allow to shoot and hit so fast that the enemy cannot defend. Now in V5, attack and defence are merged in a single roll. If my character has Celerity 4 and shoots a character without, he cannot dodge (so he doesn't roll to dodge)... But what if he wants to shoot as well?<br /> <br /> &quot;<span style=\"font-family:Cormorant\">Use before making a ranged attack. The target makes no roll to dodge or defend; make the attack at Difficulty 1. An opponent possessing Celer</span><span style=\"font-family:Cormorant\">- </span><span style=\"font-family:Cormorant\">ity 5 can nullify this power </span> <span style=\"font-family:Cormorant\">by making their own Rouse Check, defending at the same speed. </span><span style=\"font-family:inherit\">&quot;</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Defence is negated, but does this cancel his attack as well? Because in this way, as long as I don't reach hunger 5 basically I keep attacking and the enemy simply doesn't do anything... It seems a little too much even for a discipline at 4 or 5...<br /> <br /> Also... on a more generic note.<br /> When two characters attack with a gun, it is said that this assumes that they have access to a cover of some kind... otherwise the defender removes two dices from their defence roll.<br /> Now I still don't understand. If there is a duel (far west stile) with both character standing with a gun in a square, how is it resolved. Do they both remove two dices from their pool or seen that they are both attacking, this doesn't apply?<br /> As the manual keeps mentioning defence as if it was something separated from attack... but the new system seems merging the traits in a single roll.<br /> <br /> &quot;<span style=\"font-family:Cormorant\">Ranged combat is resolved as a contest, usually vs the defender\u2019s Dexterity + Athlet- ics. In cases where two combattants are attacking each other at range, you can resolve it as a two-sided </span><span style=\"font-family:Cormorant\">Firearms conflict as above. This assumes that the sub</span><span style=\"font-family:Cormorant\">- ject has access to limited cover, such as a car or the corner of a building. A character with no available cover subtracts 2 from their defense pool, whereas </span><span style=\"font-family:Cormorant\">superior cover (sandbags, concrete fortifications and </span><span style=\"font-family:Cormorant\">similar bullet-proof obstacles) merits a bonus of 1-2. </span><span style=\"font-family:inherit\">&quot;</span><br /> </span><br /> </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#050505\"><span style=\"font-family:system-ui\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\"> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\">Did I interpret this well, or did I miss something?</span><br /> </span></span></span><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26981-madquake","name":"Madquake","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26981_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-03T12:35:49-07:00","id":1456086,"title":"","content":"It's not really explained at all in the book, unfortunately. I love V5, but my one complaint is that it needed another editing pass for people to go 'hey wait, this is incomplete/badly explained'. <br /> <br /> From a balance standpoint, most STs that I've talked to (and myself included) run those two Celerity powers as follows:<ul><li>The attacker using Celerity 4/5 makes their attack roll at Difficulty 1, and the target doesn't get to roll to 'reduce' your damage, like a normal conflict roll would have. These powers are basically 'free damage' as long as you roll more than 1 success, since they can't 'defend' themselves and reduce your damage rating.</li> <li>Then the target, if their action choice was something like stabbing or shooting the attacker, rolls to try to do their damage versus the successes on the attack roll, after your damage is applied. Assuming they roll more successes than you, they can still damage you back. But it's going to be significantly less potential damage, AND you already got a huge damage drop on them (which might have dropped them outright, and via that, prevent them from attacking you back anyway).</li> </ul>As far as the 'high noon duel' thing, that's not strictly covered by the conflict rules, so you as ST is going to determine what way you want that to resolve based on the narrative. All of the conceits for ranged conflict in the book assume moving firefights, or people standing still in oncoming fire (which then is a Difficulty 1 attack against them, ala the 2 Celerity powers). Personally I'd just have it be a normal, unmodified gun pool conflict and just call it a day, there's no need for all kinds of Special Stuff for it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1808-elmerg","name":"elmerg","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"539"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-03T17:34:27-07:00","id":1456093,"title":"","content":"Hey Elmerg.<br /> It makes sense... For the Celerity one I didn't consider doing the attacks in two separate rolls...<br /> <br /> The option I thought was to roll the same way (both the attackers roll) but the one with celerity rolls at difficulty 1... So basically all of his successes enter.<br /> The opponent rolls against the successes made by the character with celerity. If he rolls more success he deals the difference in damages, if he doesn't nothing happens. The successes of the character with celerity enters as damages even if he deals less than the opponent... It seems fair and also doesn't require two different rolls...<br /> <br /> For the high noon contest, I would also do unmodified damages... Basically the attack supplies for the missing cover (both shot and can be shot... The one who hits, does also because there is no protection).<br /> The cerity one should be explained a lot better in the manual though... As a lot of people think that as long and you don't enter frenzy and do successful rouse checks, you can keep attacking without being attacked...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26981-madquake","name":"Madquake","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26981_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-04T00:38:20-07:00","id":1456106,"title":"","content":"I think this is a consequence of the Initiative-free combat and what Ex3 calls 'clashes' as the default for most attacks. It's certainly not clear and it doesn't seem that logical, either. <br /> <br /> I think Madquake's version makes the most sense, but it's still a bit janky. The 'no roll to dodge or defend' bit also seems like it needs some attention (does this include an opposing attack roll, or just defensive manoeuvres? If the latter, it's not much of a benefit to the attacker, since the target can just roll to attack instead of defending).<br /> <br /> I'd be inclined to rewrite the power altogether. <br /> <br /> Incidentally, the description is very close to that for Surprise Attacks (p.300), so it seems like the intent is that you get to make a Surprise Attack. But again, that's just an attack with Difficulty 1, when conflict is usually just 'the one with the most successes wins' rather than rolling against a strict Difficulty. <br /> <br /> For a quick alternate rule for these two powers, just say that the attacker gets to add their Celerity dots to the *successes* rolled on their attack. So it becomes that much harder to defeat them, but it's still possible. You then don't have to worry about weird interactions between the two attack rolls, Difficulty on one roll versus no Difficulty on the other, or rolling twice.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-04T09:35:40-07:00","id":1456132,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Madquake</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1456070-celerity-4-5-and-defence-in-ranged-combats?p=1456093#post1456093\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hey Elmerg.<br /> It makes sense... For the Celerity one I didn't consider doing the attacks in two separate rolls...<br /> <br /> The option I thought was to roll the same way (both the attackers roll) but the one with celerity rolls at difficulty 1... So basically all of his successes enter.<br /> The opponent rolls against the successes made by the character with celerity. If he rolls more success he deals the difference in damages, if he doesn't nothing happens. The successes of the character with celerity enters as damages even if he deals less than the opponent... It seems fair and also doesn't require two different rolls...</div> </div> </div> </div>Right. You basically just explained what I stated, in a different order (having both roll rather than having the second guy roll separately, which I do just because it's easier on some people in my group to consider them 'separate' rolls), so as long as you're good with that, it'd work.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> For the high noon contest, I would also do unmodified damages... Basically the attack supplies for the missing cover (both shot and can be shot... The one who hits, does also because there is no protection).<br /> The cerity one should be explained a lot better in the manual though... As a lot of people think that as long and you don't enter frenzy and do successful rouse checks, you can keep attacking without being attacked... </div> </div> </div>I don't disagree. The book needed another editing pass so that people could point out some stuff in there, like that or the contradictions in some initiative scales and such.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1456070-celerity-4-5-and-defence-in-ranged-combats?p=1456106#post1456106\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think Madquake's version makes the most sense, but it's still a bit janky. The 'no roll to dodge or defend' bit also seems like it needs some attention (does this include an opposing attack roll, or just defensive manoeuvres? If the latter, it's not much of a benefit to the attacker, since the target can just roll to attack instead of defending).</div> </div> </div> </div>Generally the books have used 'dodge/defend' to represent any point where you're not trying to do damage back (not just core, but expansion books too), so I run with that terminology consistency in mind.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Incidentally, the description is very close to that for Surprise Attacks (p.300), so it seems like the intent is that you get to make a Surprise Attack. But again, that's just an attack with Difficulty 1, when conflict is usually just 'the one with the most successes wins' rather than rolling against a strict Difficulty. </div> </div> </div>It is, which also has a way to avoid it with the successful noticing roll. For balance purposes, since there's no way to turn an attack with these powers into that via a 'notice' roll, and very few things deny people their actions, most people run it the above way that I've spoken with.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> For a quick alternate rule for these two powers, just say that the attacker gets to add their Celerity dots to the *successes* rolled on their attack. So it becomes that much harder to defeat them, but it's still possible. You then don't have to worry about weird interactions between the two attack rolls, Difficulty on one roll versus no Difficulty on the other, or rolling twice. </div> </div> </div>[/quote]<br /> <br /> I'm not the biggest fan of that alternative, because it would be utterly bonkers broken when combined with Prowess and maximum Potence dots (5 damage from Celerity, 5 damage from Potence, plus whatever margin, and assume Agg and not halved if Potence 5 is Fist of Caine, which it always is). That's a minimum of 11 damage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1808,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1808-elmerg","user":"elmerg","date":". 08-04-2021, 12:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1808-elmerg","name":"elmerg","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"539"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-04T11:30:05-07:00","id":1456144,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>elmerg</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1456070-celerity-4-5-and-defence-in-ranged-combats?p=1456132#post1456132\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not the biggest fan of that alternative, because it would be utterly bonkers broken when combined with Prowess and maximum Potence dots (5 damage from Celerity, 5 damage from Potence, plus whatever margin, and assume Agg and not halved if Potence 5 is Fist of Caine, which it always is). That's a minimum of 11 damage.</div> </div> </div> </div>True. I had skimmed the rules but didn't spot those interactions. My inexperience with V5 is obviously showing.<br /> <br /> I guess you could add it as dice instead. That still seems less messy than what you and Madquake suggested. But YMMV and all that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-04T17:47:36-07:00","id":1456156,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1456070-celerity-4-5-and-defence-in-ranged-combats?p=1456144#post1456144\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> True. I had skimmed the rules but didn't spot those interactions. My inexperience with V5 is obviously showing.<br /> <br /> I guess you could add it as dice instead. That still seems less messy than what you and Madquake suggested. But YMMV and all that.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Right. I was just pointing out the RAW interaction what that piece of homebrew. Honestly, the intent of the power is good (an unblockable attack that deals its full damage as long as you succeed), but it's not elegant in its current presentation. But there's not a lot you can do that leads to 'balance' points, because 'unblockable attack that denies the opponent their action/turn' is outside of most of V5's powers scopes. <br /> <br /> Adding it as dice is a decent compromise, since you are skewing the math -- but not skewing the math as bad. Though at that point, 'adding dice' also gets into other interactions like the Discipline Power Bonus, which means more dice into the pool the higher your BP. I'm gonna have to math this out and see what comes up with it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1808-elmerg","name":"elmerg","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"539"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-04T23:58:46-07:00","id":1456166,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>elmerg</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1456070-celerity-4-5-and-defence-in-ranged-combats?p=1456156#post1456156\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Right. I was just pointing out the RAW interaction what that piece of homebrew. Honestly, the intent of the power is good (an unblockable attack that deals its full damage as long as you succeed), but it's not elegant in its current presentation. But there's not a lot you can do that leads to 'balance' points, because 'unblockable attack that denies the opponent their action/turn' is outside of most of V5's powers scopes. <br /> <br /> Adding it as dice is a decent compromise, since you are skewing the math -- but not skewing the math as bad. Though at that point, 'adding dice' also gets into other interactions like the Discipline Power Bonus, which means more dice into the pool the higher your BP. I'm gonna have to math this out and see what comes up with it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, it looks like a tricky one. If you play around with it, let us know what you come up with?<br /> <br /> I think partly this is why games have always used Initiative, and V5 doesn't, so it creates some weird interactions. The RAW feels like it was written for something closer to V20 rules where combat doesn't assume a contest by default.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-05T00:45:54-07:00","id":1456168,"title":"","content":"You interpreted it well is just that V5 is a mathematical mess<br /> <br /> There is a part of the celerity rules where the game says &quot;how fast is fast?&quot; Only to answer I dunno after raising the question themselves<br /> <br /> Also there is no power levels or progresion becuase everything is randomized, why buy the first of caine to deal agg in hand to hand when random guy can buy a raufoss and deal agg+5 from the safety of his bathroom?<br /> <br /> Neither there is control from the players becuase vampires in &quot;V5&quot; are not functional beings thanks to hunger being omnipresent in a bad way becuase i like the concept but the execution is horrible","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.deviantart.com/cicerondixit/gallery\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.deviantart.com/cicerondixit/gallery</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24037-leandro16","name":"Leandro16","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24037_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-05T01:26:08-07:00","id":1456171,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leandro16</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1456070-celerity-4-5-and-defence-in-ranged-combats?p=1456168#post1456168\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You interpreted it well is just that V5 is a mathematical mess<br /> <br /> There is a part of the celerity rules where the game says &amp;quot;how fast is fast?&amp;quot; Only to answer I dunno after raising the question themselves<br /> <br /> Also there is no power levels or progresion becuase everything is randomized, why buy the first of caine to deal agg in hand to hand when random guy can buy a raufoss and deal agg+5 from the safety of his bathroom?<br /> <br /> Neither there is control from the players becuase vampires in &amp;quot;V5&amp;quot; are not functional beings thanks to hunger being omnipresent in a bad way becuase i like the concept but the execution is horrible</div> </div> </div> </div>I think V5 isn't the only RPG to rush to meet an arbitrary deadline, and then has come out with muddled rules as a result. WFRP4e did this, too, although it is still often clearer than V5.<br /> <br /> I think all RPGs need an open playtest period to iron out mistakes and increase clarity. But I know that's not always feasible. OPP manages this quite well with their Kickstarters (it's not to the degree of PF2e or anything, but it's enough to avoid most of the howlers).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-05T02:16:27-07:00","id":1456172,"title":"","content":"I asked on FB too, in a group, and they explained that in this case the action is divided into two...<br /> Basically, the vampire that uses celerity rolls at difficult 1 and the opponent doesn't.... then the opponent attacks the vampire (with a separate roll) and the vampire tries to defend with a dodge (not an attack).<br /> <br /> Basically it grants the vampire an extra free attack and the main action for him becomes a pure defensive one... It kinda makes more sense...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26981-madquake","name":"Madquake","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26981_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-05T23:37:10-07:00","id":1456216,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Madquake</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1456070-celerity-4-5-and-defence-in-ranged-combats?p=1456172#post1456172\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I asked on FB too, in a group, and they explained that in this case the action is divided into two...<br /> Basically, the vampire that uses celerity rolls at difficult 1 and the opponent doesn't.... then the opponent attacks the vampire (with a separate roll) and the vampire tries to defend with a dodge (not an attack).<br /> <br /> Basically it grants the vampire an extra free attack and the main action for him becomes a pure defensive one... It kinda makes more sense...</div> </div> </div> </div>That makes the most sense yet, yes. And it's a brief explanation, too, which is useful! Thank you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}